WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:04.890
Welcome back to our second drink of Niagara Part 2.

2
00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:09.250
Jenna, you have some amazing location breakdowns in this episode.

3
00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:12.730
And there's even more great details from Randy Cordray

4
00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:16.970
about that deleted storyline of the horse going over the falls.

5
00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:19.570
I was very proud of my fast facts for this episode.

6
00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:20.490
You should be.

7
00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.790
But you know, there's one thing I didn't share

8
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:24.830
because there was just so much to discuss.

9
00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:28.250
And that was the ratings for this episode.

10
00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:34.650
9.42 million households in America tuned in to watch Niagara Part 2.

11
00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:38.350
It was the second highest viewed episode of the season.

12
00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:40.650
Can you guess what the highest was?

13
00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:44.650
I mean, I would probably guess delivery because they're having a baby.

14
00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:45.290
Yes.

15
00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:45.770
Okay.

16
00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:46.710
Yes.

17
00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:48.970
But you know, that's pretty cool.

18
00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:53.510
Nine, over 9 million people watched it on the day it aired.

19
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:54.210
I know.

20
00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:55.310
That is really cool.

21
00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:57.810
Well, I have a fun fan letter to share.

22
00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:00.570
Remember when we first broke down the Niagara episodes,

23
00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:02.690
I had traded messages with Joya,

24
00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:06.050
who worked at NBC Digital about Jim and Pam's wedding website?

25
00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:06.550
Yes.

26
00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:07.010
Okay.

27
00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:11.410
Well, Jenna, you shared that NBC asked you to do like a fakie registry

28
00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:13.830
for a few things on the wedding website.

29
00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:15.850
We talked about it a little bit,

30
00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:19.390
but that brings me to this letter from Nyla in Maryland.

31
00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:21.050
Nyla says,

32
00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:23.390
Hello from Maryland, office ladies.

33
00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.510
I loved your breakdown of this episode.

34
00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:27.210
I have never written to you before,

35
00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:30.510
but I wanted to share that when you first talked about this episode,

36
00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:33.430
I was getting married and planning my wedding.

37
00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:36.970
I was so curious about Jim and Pam's wedding website

38
00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:39.570
that I went to the website you shared on Instagram,

39
00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:43.810
and I was so surprised to see what Jim and Pam put on their registry.

40
00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:48.150
They registered for two items that I also registered for.

41
00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:49.230
Okay.

42
00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:56.230
So now, lady, Nyla did not list what she and Jim and Pam all, I guess, put on their registry.

43
00:01:56.490 --> 00:02:00.010
So I went back to the official website that NBC made,

44
00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:03.010
and I'm guessing the two things.

45
00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:03.510
Okay.

46
00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.530
Because here's what Jim registered for.

47
00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:09.830
One Alice Crystal Pitcher, which they got.

48
00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:12.570
Oh, by the way, it tells you if they got it or not.

49
00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:17.330
One set of Oneida Chateau Flatware set, 46 pieces.

50
00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:19.050
They also got that.

51
00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:19.410
Okay.

52
00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:22.690
One Porsche 911 Carrera.

53
00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:24.630
They did not get that.

54
00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:24.950
Okay.

55
00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:29.130
So, Nyla, I'm guessing you also registered for a picture in Flatware.

56
00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:32.470
Anyway, Nyla goes on to say,

57
00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:37.290
But ladies, did you see what Jim and Pam wrote on their registry page?

58
00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:39.350
I feel like it needs to be discussed.

59
00:02:39.710 --> 00:02:43.610
Why do they have such a big mortgage if it was Jim's parents' house?

60
00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:47.190
So, again, Jenna, I was curious.

61
00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:49.510
When we first broke down this episode,

62
00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:52.630
I had shared Jim and Pam's guest book entries on the website,

63
00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:54.910
but I didn't dive into their actual registry.

64
00:02:54.910 --> 00:02:56.530
I didn't go into any of that.

65
00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.430
So, here's what Nyla's talking about.

66
00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:03.450
Jim and Pam had a message to their wedding guests on their website that said,

67
00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:04.070
Quote,

68
00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:08.750
Hello, everyone, and thanks for thinking about us by checking out our registry.

69
00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:12.650
Jim and I already have most everything we need for our new house.

70
00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:14.610
And then in parentheses, it says,

71
00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:17.850
The one with the big mortgage that we bought at the height of the market.

72
00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:21.050
And then it goes on to say,

73
00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:23.610
We registered for some items listed on the link below.

74
00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:26.630
If everything's been gifted and you still want to get us something,

75
00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:31.910
we'd prefer you send a financial contribution instead of items that aren't on the registry.

76
00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:33.030
Winky face.

77
00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:35.190
Looking forward to seeing you at our wedding.

78
00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:37.570
In parentheses, the one that's way over budget.

79
00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:39.390
Two exclamation points.

80
00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:39.910
Thanks.

81
00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:42.650
I'm speechless.

82
00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:43.410
I know.

83
00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:44.510
Why?

84
00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:45.930
They didn't even get a good deal?

85
00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:47.150
They didn't get a good deal.

86
00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:52.510
Well, and Jim snagged it at the height of the market and his parents really gouged him.

87
00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:53.630
I mean, wow.

88
00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:54.290
I know.

89
00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:57.870
And also, it sounds like they're paying for their own wedding.

90
00:03:58.090 --> 00:03:59.250
Which is over budget.

91
00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:02.350
Anyway, I found that all really fascinating.

92
00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:07.050
Nyla, thanks for writing in and leading me to dig a little deeper there.

93
00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:13.170
Well, now I'm surprised that they even had $10,000 for Jim to put into Athlete in the first place.

94
00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:13.350
Oh, my gosh.

95
00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:16.010
How did they even get any money in savings at this point?

96
00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:16.430
I don't know.

97
00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:16.910
I'm impressed.

98
00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:19.710
I love that you always bring it back to Athlete.

99
00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:27.390
I mean, I'm still so sore that he put our money in that business without talking to me.

100
00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:29.670
I can't let it go.

101
00:04:30.130 --> 00:04:31.070
Oh, everyone.

102
00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:33.070
Thank you so much for writing in.

103
00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:34.350
We love hearing from you.

104
00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:37.650
And now, here is your second drink of Niagara Part 2.

105
00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:42.740
I'm Jenna Fisher.

106
00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:44.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.

107
00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:45.340
We were on The Office together.

108
00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:46.600
And we're best friends.

109
00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:50.400
And now, we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.

110
00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:57.380
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.

111
00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:58.540
We're the Office ladies.

112
00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:02.680
Angela, Angela.

113
00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:04.640
Jutta, Jutta.

114
00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:07.780
Today is Jim and Pam's wedding day.

115
00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.880
And we are celebrating.

116
00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:10.940
Cheers.

117
00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:12.540
That's my drink.

118
00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:13.520
Can you hear it?

119
00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:14.620
I sure can.

120
00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.280
I'm taking a picture of you.

121
00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:17.200
Okay.

122
00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:24.220
Well, if you take a picture, we can post this on Office Ladies Pod because I'm drinking out of a very special champagne flute.

123
00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:25.880
Tell them all about it.

124
00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:26.720
It is...

125
00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.800
Jenna, can I say it's craptastic?

126
00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:32.720
It is the kitschiest thing you've ever seen in your life.

127
00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:41.320
It is a champagne flute, but the stem is a series of four glass hearts.

128
00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.760
That are, like, hollow in the middle.

129
00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:45.520
Yes.

130
00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:48.600
And it's a very large champagne flute.

131
00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:52.400
I didn't have any champagne, so I'm actually drinking an old-fashioned out of it.

132
00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:53.340
Is that weird?

133
00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:55.440
I think it's flippin' perfect.

134
00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:56.260
Thank you.

135
00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:57.080
Cheers to you.

136
00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:58.960
I wish we were in the same room today.

137
00:05:59.200 --> 00:05:59.680
Dang it.

138
00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:00.640
I know.

139
00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:03.460
You've got a glass of red wine, though, so...

140
00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:04.920
I came to Earwolf today.

141
00:06:05.020 --> 00:06:10.400
I said, Sam, Jenna is pouring an old-fashioned into her Niagara champagne flute.

142
00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:11.300
What do we got here?

143
00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:13.280
And he goes, I think there's some stuff over there.

144
00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:20.300
I found a bottle of red wine and a croissant, so I'm feeling very fancy.

145
00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:23.900
You're very European, I think, red wine and a croissant.

146
00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:25.580
I feel like I am.

147
00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:28.860
Well, let me tell you where I got this champagne flute.

148
00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:37.300
When we traveled to Niagara Falls to shoot this episode, the hotel put a basket in my hotel room

149
00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:46.300
with these two champagne flutes, champagne, chocolates, candies, nuts, like a whole welcome

150
00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:52.320
basket, and they were just so delighted that the office had come to shoot there, and I was

151
00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:54.160
so charmed by that.

152
00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:57.760
I thought it was the sweetest gesture, and so I ate all the food.

153
00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:02.260
I actually shared it with the hair and makeup ladies, and I took the champagne glasses home,

154
00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:05.360
and now here they are in all their glory.

155
00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:06.540
Yum.

156
00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:08.960
Jenna, I love this story so much.

157
00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:12.300
You are truly my BFF, because I would have done the same thing.

158
00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:14.880
I would have been like, um, these glasses are going home with me.

159
00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:19.220
Oh yeah, lady, I wrapped these up in a t-shirt, and I packed them in my suitcase.

160
00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:21.300
It's amazing, we have to post it in stories.

161
00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:24.800
You guys, Niagara Part 2, we're here to break it down for you.

162
00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:25.740
That's right.

163
00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:27.940
This is Season 6, Episode 5.

164
00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:32.780
It was written by Greg Daniels and Mindy Kaling, and directed by Paul Feig.

165
00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:36.280
Let me give you a summary of what we'll be going over today.

166
00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:43.140
Last night, Andy slept on Pam's floor, because he was recovering from his torn scrotum.

167
00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:43.740
Mm-hmm.

168
00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:46.440
Michael slept by the vending machines.

169
00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:49.240
Dwight hooked up with Pam's friend.

170
00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:52.700
And Kevin is about to lose his shoes.

171
00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:57.460
How's that for, like, a headline?

172
00:07:57.800 --> 00:07:58.380
That's good.

173
00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:04.240
The wedding, which is happening today, is becoming even more hectic than enjoyable for Pam and Jim,

174
00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:07.320
and ultimately, they're going to take matters into their own hands.

175
00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:15.660
Meanwhile, Michael makes an unlikely love connection, and the office gang surprised Jim and Pam with a celebratory dance.

176
00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:18.140
I love this episode so much.

177
00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:24.860
I know we both have said that, but this second part of Niagara is when all the, like, heartstrings are pulled.

178
00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.940
I mean, it's so beautiful and cringy.

179
00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:28.820
It's fantastic.

180
00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:32.500
We had Greg Daniels on for Niagara Part 1.

181
00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:34.380
We talked about the whole entire episode.

182
00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:37.440
So if you guys haven't heard that interview, listen to it.

183
00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:39.320
Now we're going to break down the second part.

184
00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:40.980
We have lots of fun stuff to share.

185
00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:48.760
This second part of Niagara also features the part where Jim and Pam sneak off and have a wedding ceremony on Maid of the MiSt.

186
00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.440
That is my fastback number one.

187
00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:54.560
We got a fan question from Ashlyn M.

188
00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:55.620
in Windsor, Canada.

189
00:08:56.120 --> 00:09:01.040
Did everyone get to go on location to Niagara Falls, or was it just Jenna and John?

190
00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:06.100
Did you stay on the American side, or did you get to go to the Canadian side as well?

191
00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:17.160
Well, like we said last week, Ashlyn, we shot the rehearsal dinner and the church wedding and the bulk of this episode in Los Angeles.

192
00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:25.580
The only people who went to Niagara Falls were me, John Krasinski, Mindy, Randy Cordray, who was our line producer,

193
00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:31.720
our cinematographer, Randall Einhorn, our director, Paul Feig, and then a handful of crew members.

194
00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:35.700
And we went to the American side of Niagara Falls.

195
00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:40.500
And we only had, Angela, one day to shoot.

196
00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:41.680
One day.

197
00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:43.260
One day to get all of that?

198
00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:44.040
Yes.

199
00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:47.420
And I'm going to tell you now a little bit about how it all went down,

200
00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:51.200
because Randy had to do an insane amount of preparation to get us there.

201
00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:52.260
He sure did.

202
00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:54.920
And he shared with us, you guys, we're going to break it down for you.

203
00:09:54.920 --> 00:10:07.740
You know, originally, the network said that they wanted John and I to shoot this on a green screen at, like, a fake water tank on, like, a fakie boat in Los Angeles.

204
00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:08.440
Boo!

205
00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:09.120
Boo!

206
00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:10.020
Right?

207
00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:10.780
Yeah!

208
00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:14.120
Randy was like, no, no.

209
00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:15.480
So...

210
00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:16.560
Good for Randy.

211
00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:17.440
Yeah.

212
00:10:17.980 --> 00:10:23.820
So Randy set out to create a budget that the network would approve for me and John to actually go.

213
00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:29.800
Now, Greg told Randy that he would like us to shoot on the Canadian side of the falls,

214
00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:36.340
because that's the side that has all the fun, kind of kitschy wax museums and the water park.

215
00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:40.240
And it had the look that Greg was going for.

216
00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:41.740
On the Canadian side?

217
00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:43.220
On the Canadian side.

218
00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:43.700
Okay.

219
00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:50.440
But Randy found out that Canada has this very strict one-for-one staffing rule.

220
00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:59.160
And what that means is for every person that he brought from our crew, he would have to hire a Canadian to do a job.

221
00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:05.760
So if we wanted to bring our regular makeup artist, we would have to hire someone locally, you know, for a different job.

222
00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:13.000
It didn't have to be another makeup artist, but just there had to be like a one-for-one representation on this crew.

223
00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:14.020
Oh.

224
00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:15.980
We did not have the budget for that.

225
00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:16.720
Got it.

226
00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:21.820
He also said that Canada has a 14-day embargo on all equipment.

227
00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:27.820
So any costumes, cameras, props, we would have to send it 14 days ahead of time.

228
00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:32.340
Well, we couldn't do that because we were using all that stuff in Los Angeles.

229
00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:33.100
Right.

230
00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:36.100
So Randy got this approved.

231
00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:36.820
Great.

232
00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:41.300
We had the budget to shoot on the American side of the falls, but then there was a problem.

233
00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:45.700
The Maid of the Mist, it's in, like, dual waters.

234
00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:54.000
Also, the Maid of the Mist is owned by a Canadian company, so that was a whole thing that Randy had to work out.

235
00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:59.560
That's right, because he said they leave Canada and then cross over into American waters.

236
00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:00.060
Yes.

237
00:12:00.140 --> 00:12:01.460
But then they go back to Canada.

238
00:12:01.460 --> 00:12:02.300
Right.

239
00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:10.860
But then they do have a boat that will start on the American side or will pick up Americans and go back to the Canadian side.

240
00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:16.920
So you can ride it from the American side, but there's limited access to those rides.

241
00:12:17.140 --> 00:12:19.300
Most of the rides start on the Canadian side.

242
00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:20.500
It was a whole thing.

243
00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:22.980
This is so complicated for a boat ride.

244
00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:35.240
I mean, while I was in my hotel room with my fancy champagne glasses, I had no idea everything that had gone on to get me there to that gift basket.

245
00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:35.820
Wow.

246
00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:41.880
Randy shared with us that there were a lot of people that made this amazing moment happen for Jim and Pam.

247
00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:44.580
We promised him we would give them a shout out.

