280
00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:34.720
The minister looks up and stops.

281
00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:40.660
The camera whips over to see a man leading a horse into the space.

282
00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:44.060
On top of the horse is Roy, dressed in a suit.

283
00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:48.040
I have to point out, Roy didn't even ride the horse into the church.

284
00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:50.660
He had like a guy bring him in?

285
00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.060
He has a guy leading him.

286
00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:55.260
Like someone is holding the reins, walking him in.

287
00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:57.360
Roy yells, wait!

288
00:14:58.240 --> 00:15:00.740
Pam has a horrified expression.

289
00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:07.400
Everyone is staring, shocked at Roy, who tries to keep the horse pointed at Pam, but the handler

290
00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:09.580
struggles to keep it pointed the right way.

291
00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:12.600
So, like, Roy has no command over this horse at all.

292
00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:16.820
The horse's tail whips by Stanley's face, who looks annoyed.

293
00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:21.280
Jim whispers to himself, holy f***.

294
00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:22.280
What?

295
00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:24.980
They had an F-bomb?

296
00:15:25.140 --> 00:15:26.260
They had an F-bomb.

297
00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:33.420
Roy says, Pammy, we lived together for nine years and did everything a man and wife do.

298
00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:36.520
Camera pans over to Meemaw.

299
00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:39.280
Pam is horribly uncomfortable.

300
00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:47.160
Roy, you loved me once, and can you imagine ever seeing me again as your knight on a white horse or a brown horse?

301
00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:49.200
People change, and I have too.

302
00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:53.880
If you have any second thoughts, any at all, don't do this thing.

303
00:15:55.020 --> 00:15:57.380
Pam, I don't have any second thoughts, Roy.

304
00:15:57.540 --> 00:15:58.720
I love Jim, not you.

305
00:15:58.880 --> 00:16:00.920
I wish you had just called firSt.

306
00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:05.850
Long, awkward pause.

307
00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:09.790
Then Roy says, then I will leave you with this thought.

308
00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:11.310
You're making a mistake.

309
00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:13.950
Jim, seriously, man?

310
00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:16.170
Roy, get me out of here.

311
00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:18.970
That's what he says to the handler of the horse.

312
00:16:19.610 --> 00:16:22.150
Jim, you could have learned to ride it, you know.

313
00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:23.590
That would have been a little less.

314
00:16:23.770 --> 00:16:25.310
And then Pam goes, Jim, Jim, Jim.

315
00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:30.190
The handler walks the horse away as Roy tries to keep his dignity.

316
00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:32.590
Oscar booze, boo.

317
00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:37.570
And then the minister says, okay, where were we?

318
00:16:38.090 --> 00:16:42.370
He starts them back into their vows, but the camera pans over to Dwight.

319
00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:48.330
Dwight is seated next to a wedding guest and says, that is a powerful-looking horse.

320
00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:49.010
Excuse me.

321
00:16:49.170 --> 00:16:50.330
He gets an idea.

322
00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:52.770
He gets up and follows Roy out.

323
00:16:53.850 --> 00:16:54.330
Wow.

324
00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:56.070
Wow.

325
00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:56.770
Yeah.

326
00:16:56.970 --> 00:17:00.610
And then the other scenes are the ones Greg talked about, where Dwight convinces Roy to let

327
00:17:00.610 --> 00:17:01.750
him return the horse.

328
00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:07.550
But then, because he's seen all of this, like, historical footage of animals that can go over

329
00:17:07.550 --> 00:17:12.010
the falls and survive, Dwight then tries to ride the horse over the falls, but then he

330
00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:12.510
bails.

331
00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:15.190
EMS, like, rescues Dwight.

332
00:17:15.290 --> 00:17:17.090
But the horse goes over, but the horse survives.

333
00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:18.510
Yeah.

334
00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:20.830
It was a crazy storyline.

335
00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:23.810
And Greg shared that they did end up cutting this.

336
00:17:24.490 --> 00:17:28.910
But one thing Greg said in his interview really piqued my curiosity.

337
00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:33.950
I mean, there were so many things, but he said that, you know, this storyline wasn't

338
00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:38.210
cut until the table read, which is about one week before we started shooting.

339
00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:39.310
Oh, yeah.

340
00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:41.450
So we were very close to shooting.

341
00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:47.050
And this entire time, Randy had been prepping this episode as if a horse was going to go

342
00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:47.830
over the falls.

343
00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:54.830
And Greg even said, like, they went to Universal Studios and they saw a demonstration of a water

344
00:17:54.830 --> 00:17:58.510
tank and how the horse might fall into the water tank.

345
00:17:58.510 --> 00:17:59.630
And I was like, what?

346
00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:02.730
So I reached out to Randy Cordray.

347
00:18:03.550 --> 00:18:10.070
Angela, I have to share with you how much prep he did on this horse scene that was cut.

348
00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:11.670
I find it fascinating.

349
00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:18.530
I still can't get over the fact that this horse story was a go until about seven days before

350
00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:19.110
we shot.

351
00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:20.110
I know.

352
00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:21.210
All right.

353
00:18:21.310 --> 00:18:24.570
Here's the first thing that Randy said to me, and I'm going to quote him.

354
00:18:24.570 --> 00:18:25.430
He said,

355
00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:30.190
I had never been asked to create a scene of such complexity and magnitude.

356
00:18:30.530 --> 00:18:36.250
This was far beyond the scope of creating the rainy proposal rest stop or throwing a

357
00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:42.270
fake cat into the ceiling or adding a soccer ball careening off of Phyllis's head or producing

358
00:18:42.270 --> 00:18:44.830
a Cloris Leachman Jack Black mini movie.

359
00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:52.090
I was fearful that our meager television budget was far too small to produce the needed quality

360
00:18:52.090 --> 00:18:55.270
to make this gag appear credible and above all funny.

361
00:18:55.830 --> 00:19:01.750
But he said, nonetheless, he moved forward as that was what he had to do.

362
00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:10.390
So he said the first thing he had to do was find a church in Los Angeles that could fit

363
00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:12.010
a horse through its front doors.

364
00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:14.710
That's how we picked the church?

365
00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:19.010
Yeah, because Roy had to come in riding a horse.

366
00:19:19.190 --> 00:19:25.270
So not just big enough to fit a horse, but fit a man on a horse through the front doors.

367
00:19:25.610 --> 00:19:27.590
And I guess a man leading a horse.

368
00:19:29.590 --> 00:19:31.210
Imagine that, Scout.

369
00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:33.070
Imagine that.

370
00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:34.810
Are you just measuring church doors?

371
00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:37.650
And then the people are like, what are you measuring for?

372
00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:42.550
This makes the church choice make sense to me now because it was one level.

373
00:19:42.710 --> 00:19:45.830
There weren't like multiple steps you had to go up to get to the front door.

374
00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:47.470
And they had two big doors.

375
00:19:47.770 --> 00:19:48.150
Yeah.

376
00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:49.750
For the horse.

377
00:19:49.990 --> 00:19:51.070
For the horse.

378
00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:52.570
All right.

379
00:19:52.970 --> 00:19:55.430
Then he went to Stargate International.

380
00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:57.350
They were our go-to effects company.

381
00:19:57.890 --> 00:20:03.250
He was going to have to create the element of rushing water.

382
00:20:03.250 --> 00:20:09.970
He was going to have to have Dwight on the horse riding into that rushing water, Dwight bailing

383
00:20:09.970 --> 00:20:17.890
off the horse and being rescued, and then like a series of the horse in various poses to

384
00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:19.930
simulate tumbling down the falls.

385
00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:21.230
Oh, my gosh.

386
00:20:21.230 --> 00:20:27.890
And then Stargate would have to be able to composite all of these and put them behind Jim and Pam

387
00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:30.730
in the waterfall as they're getting married.

388
00:20:31.570 --> 00:20:33.990
Randy said the costs were astronomical.

389
00:20:34.490 --> 00:20:37.810
I was going to say, I think our ending had to have been cheaper.

390
00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:45.250
He said he reached out to Universal Studios' back lot because they have a location there

391
00:20:45.250 --> 00:20:50.530
called Lower Falls Lake, which is basically that tank that Greg was talking about.

392
00:20:50.530 --> 00:20:51.950
It has an enormous green screen.

393
00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:56.390
It can be filled with warm water to a depth of about eight feet.

394
00:20:57.290 --> 00:21:03.370
But in order to make the water churn, like to simulate the rushing water of the Niagara

395
00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:11.370
River, their plan was to chain four jet skis to the side of the tank, which would then

396
00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:14.190
run and create like a whitewater effect.

397
00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:16.270
So like, listen to everything.

398
00:21:16.270 --> 00:21:18.350
He's like, I need four jet ski drivers.

399
00:21:19.110 --> 00:21:24.810
Then he had to contact the animal service company to talk about the horse and get this.

400
00:21:24.990 --> 00:21:26.150
I did not know this.

401
00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:31.510
Randy learned that you need a special stunt horse because horses actually don't like to

402
00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:37.130
walk in water on their own because they don't like to walk or run anywhere where they can't

403
00:21:37.130 --> 00:21:38.030
see their hooves.

404
00:21:38.530 --> 00:21:43.450
And he said, when you see horses in a Western movie, like dashing across a river, those are

405
00:21:43.450 --> 00:21:44.610
specially trained horses.

406
00:21:44.610 --> 00:21:47.210
So they had to like start that process immediately.

407
00:21:48.230 --> 00:21:49.510
Yeah, that makes sense.

408
00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.050
So we've got our jet ski drivers.

409
00:21:52.050 --> 00:21:54.370
We're training the horse to go into water.

410
00:21:55.050 --> 00:22:01.330
But for the digital element of the horse tumbling, he said they were going to have to put a horse

411
00:22:01.330 --> 00:22:10.230
into like a green screen harness and then lift the horse on a construction crane against a green

412
00:22:10.230 --> 00:22:18.390
screen and then have a camera crew like shoot like 360 degrees around the horse so they could

413
00:22:18.390 --> 00:22:21.030
then make it look like it was tumbling.

414
00:22:21.350 --> 00:22:22.670
Like it would be a visual effect.

415
00:22:22.770 --> 00:22:26.010
They would never tumble the horse, but they do have to suspend the horse.

416
00:22:26.170 --> 00:22:27.050
Sure, sure, sure.

417
00:22:27.050 --> 00:22:33.190
He said this also required like many weeks of training and preparation to make sure that

418
00:22:33.190 --> 00:22:36.310
the horse was not stressed, that it was OK being lifted up.

419
00:22:36.410 --> 00:22:37.930
So this whole time.

420
00:22:38.210 --> 00:22:38.410
Yeah.

421
00:22:38.550 --> 00:22:39.990
There was a horse actor.

422
00:22:40.470 --> 00:22:40.730
Right.

423
00:22:40.850 --> 00:22:47.730
Learning how to get comfortable in water and being suspended in a harness from a crane.

424
00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:49.310
Yeah, that horse was prepping.

425
00:22:49.530 --> 00:22:50.430
Oh, bless its heart.

426
00:22:50.890 --> 00:22:51.150
Yes.

427
00:22:51.810 --> 00:22:58.130
Then Randy had to find a stunt double for Rain because obviously Rain did not want to ride

428
00:22:58.130 --> 00:23:00.970
a horse into a tank of rushing water and jump off of it.

429
00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:04.770
So they had to find a special stunt double for Rain.

430
00:23:05.250 --> 00:23:08.990
But he said they still needed close ups of Rain's face.

431
00:23:08.990 --> 00:23:12.090
So they were going to have to do that facial replacement effect.

432
00:23:12.370 --> 00:23:13.810
Oh, my gosh.

433
00:23:13.810 --> 00:23:17.110
Where they replaced the stuntman's face with Rain's face.

434
00:23:17.730 --> 00:23:18.430
All right.

435
00:23:18.690 --> 00:23:26.470
In the end, Randy estimated that this two part episode with the church and the hotel and

436
00:23:26.470 --> 00:23:32.230
the Niagara and the cast and the extras and animals and all the horse stuff, it was going

437
00:23:32.230 --> 00:23:35.430
to be about a million dollars more than our usual budget.

438
00:23:35.910 --> 00:23:37.130
Oh, my gosh.

439
00:23:37.650 --> 00:23:41.130
And NBC said you can only have half that.

440
00:23:41.710 --> 00:23:43.690
And he was like, I can't do it all.

441
00:23:44.330 --> 00:23:49.130
Oh, on top of that, I forgot to tell you, Allison Jones told him David Denman is not

442
00:23:49.130 --> 00:23:49.490
available.

443
00:23:49.670 --> 00:23:51.010
He's shooting a movie in New Orleans.

444
00:23:51.210 --> 00:23:52.350
They will not let him leave.

445
00:23:52.530 --> 00:23:57.330
So they were also like trying to fight with this movie company to get David Denman out

446
00:23:57.330 --> 00:24:00.170
for a day so he could ride this horse into the church.

447
00:24:00.810 --> 00:24:05.070
Do you realize how happy Randy was when this gag got pulled?

