01:02:44.360 --> 01:02:47.620
I remember standing back there with you before it was my turn.

1237
01:02:48.220 --> 01:02:49.140
Yeah, yeah.

1238
01:02:49.760 --> 01:02:54.900
Well, Marianne Kellogg, who choreographed Cafe Disco, also helped choreograph the dancing

1239
01:02:54.900 --> 01:02:55.640
down the aisle.

1240
01:02:56.060 --> 01:02:59.880
Parts of it were choreographed and part was like freestyle, you know?

1241
01:03:00.260 --> 01:03:00.420
Yeah.

1242
01:03:00.520 --> 01:03:01.660
A little bit of a combination.

1243
01:03:02.340 --> 01:03:08.700
I remember talking to Paul Feig about Angela Martin, and we both sort of felt like she wouldn't

1244
01:03:08.700 --> 01:03:10.080
dance in a church.

1245
01:03:10.720 --> 01:03:14.460
But yet she would want to participate if everyone was participating.

1246
01:03:14.960 --> 01:03:17.620
She wouldn't just be sitting in a pew watching.

1247
01:03:17.960 --> 01:03:21.700
So I said to him, what if Angela Martin walks down clutching her purse?

1248
01:03:21.800 --> 01:03:24.120
Because I also don't think she'd leave her purse unattended.

1249
01:03:25.140 --> 01:03:26.580
These are great details.

1250
01:03:26.900 --> 01:03:27.080
Yeah.

1251
01:03:27.260 --> 01:03:29.000
So he really liked that.

1252
01:03:29.200 --> 01:03:33.500
And so that's why Angela Martin just walks down the aisle looking at everyone holding

1253
01:03:33.500 --> 01:03:34.100
her purse.

1254
01:03:34.460 --> 01:03:36.880
We got a fan question from Peyton H.

1255
01:03:36.960 --> 01:03:40.620
in Vermont who said, how many takes did you do to get

1256
01:03:40.620 --> 01:03:41.260
this right?

1257
01:03:42.020 --> 01:03:45.760
You guys, it was one take.

1258
01:03:46.820 --> 01:03:54.440
Randy Cordray shared with us that because this was such a last-minute idea and we had so little

1259
01:03:54.440 --> 01:04:00.080
time at the church, we only had enough time to do this dance scene twice.

1260
01:04:00.820 --> 01:04:07.660
We could do two takes of it, but everybody nailed it on the first take, so we moved on.

1261
01:04:08.460 --> 01:04:15.000
I was also in touch, lady, with Tug Coker, who plays one of Jim's brothers, and he has

1262
01:04:15.000 --> 01:04:17.600
a crazy story about doing this dance sequence.

1263
01:04:17.760 --> 01:04:18.720
So here's the thing.

1264
01:04:18.840 --> 01:04:26.120
We did one full take, like one running long take of this, but within that, we did several

1265
01:04:26.120 --> 01:04:27.720
takes of each bit.

1266
01:04:27.720 --> 01:04:28.280
Right.

1267
01:04:28.440 --> 01:04:32.020
We would reset really quickly depending on who was in the aisle.

1268
01:04:32.540 --> 01:04:32.960
Yes.

1269
01:04:33.200 --> 01:04:37.520
So Paul Feig, I guess, told Tug, here's what I want you to do.

1270
01:04:38.380 --> 01:04:44.460
I want you to dance down the aisle, and then once you're off camera, run around the back

1271
01:04:44.460 --> 01:04:49.220
outside of the church, through the courtyard, back to the front of the church, and go down

1272
01:04:49.220 --> 01:04:49.980
the aisle again.

1273
01:04:50.300 --> 01:04:50.920
That's right.

1274
01:04:51.000 --> 01:04:52.120
We had to do that, you guys.

1275
01:04:52.220 --> 01:04:55.860
As soon as we did our individual pass, then we had to run back so we could do the group

1276
01:04:55.860 --> 01:04:56.300
pass.

1277
01:04:56.780 --> 01:05:02.420
So Tug said he did a couple of laps where he just danced individually down the aisle,

1278
01:05:02.480 --> 01:05:06.260
and then they would hold, and he would run, and he would do his individual dance down

1279
01:05:06.260 --> 01:05:07.620
the aisle, and then he would run.

1280
01:05:08.020 --> 01:05:11.660
And he said, and then he also had to run to get into the group formation.

1281
01:05:12.660 --> 01:05:18.820
He said, well, one of the times when he turned the corner from the courtyard, he slipped in

1282
01:05:18.820 --> 01:05:22.900
his dress shoes, and he just wiped out in front of the whole caSt.

1283
01:05:23.000 --> 01:05:25.080
He said he almost took down Ed HelMs.

1284
01:05:25.240 --> 01:05:25.840
Oh, no.

1285
01:05:26.320 --> 01:05:28.080
He said he was in a lot of pain.

1286
01:05:28.540 --> 01:05:32.980
He went to the doctor and found out he had badly sprained his wriSt.

1287
01:05:33.160 --> 01:05:36.820
He had to get a splint after we wrapped the episode.

1288
01:05:37.240 --> 01:05:39.080
He must have been really hurting.

1289
01:05:39.780 --> 01:05:40.140
Yes.

1290
01:05:40.540 --> 01:05:44.020
He said he fell, and he did that thing, you know, like, where you're like, I'm fine.

1291
01:05:44.080 --> 01:05:44.400
I'm fine.

1292
01:05:44.420 --> 01:05:46.140
I'll just continue dancing down the aisle.

1293
01:05:46.220 --> 01:05:51.080
But, like, as soon as the take was over, he, like, went to the doctor, and he was really

1294
01:05:51.080 --> 01:05:51.420
hurt.

1295
01:05:51.600 --> 01:05:56.480
So when we got back in touch, he was like, Jenna, Jenna, when you get to the Niagara episode,

1296
01:05:56.500 --> 01:05:57.680
I've got a story.

1297
01:05:58.640 --> 01:06:00.180
You've got to hear this story.

1298
01:06:00.780 --> 01:06:05.080
And listen, lady, Tug wasn't the only person who wanted to tell us a story about dancing

1299
01:06:05.080 --> 01:06:06.140
down the aisle at a wedding.

1300
01:06:06.300 --> 01:06:08.760
We also got some fan mail from Kate S.

1301
01:06:08.940 --> 01:06:09.600
in Virginia.

1302
01:06:10.320 --> 01:06:11.780
Here is what she said.

1303
01:06:12.040 --> 01:06:16.460
I have been waiting for this episode to tell you ladies this great story.

1304
01:06:17.340 --> 01:06:21.980
I was a bridesmaid in a wedding where the bride wanted us to dance into the reception

1305
01:06:21.980 --> 01:06:25.460
like the office crew danced down the aisle at Jim and Pam's wedding.

1306
01:06:25.460 --> 01:06:30.760
The other bridesmaids were not really into it, but being the office lover I am, I knew

1307
01:06:30.760 --> 01:06:32.360
this was my moment to shine.

1308
01:06:33.000 --> 01:06:35.660
I started by walking like Phyllis.

1309
01:06:36.080 --> 01:06:38.340
Then I broke into Oscar's pivot.

1310
01:06:39.040 --> 01:06:41.960
Then I wanted to do the infamous Dwight kick.

1311
01:06:42.140 --> 01:06:45.320
But my foot slipped, and I fell immediately forward.

1312
01:06:45.600 --> 01:06:48.040
My face broke my fall.

1313
01:06:48.240 --> 01:06:49.140
Oh, no!

1314
01:06:49.740 --> 01:06:51.880
She said, I was so embarrassed.

1315
01:06:51.880 --> 01:06:57.820
I jumped right up, ran to the dance floor behind everyone, and as soon as the bride and

1316
01:06:57.820 --> 01:07:02.720
groom came out, I ran to the bathroom because my face was covered in blood and I was missing

1317
01:07:02.720 --> 01:07:03.800
my front tooth.

1318
01:07:03.980 --> 01:07:05.420
Oh, my gosh!

1319
01:07:05.880 --> 01:07:09.420
But she said it was all for the love of the office.

1320
01:07:09.760 --> 01:07:11.160
Oh, my gosh.

1321
01:07:11.720 --> 01:07:14.820
Kate, you waited so long to send us that piece of mail.

1322
01:07:14.820 --> 01:07:16.320
Well, I just had to read it.

1323
01:07:16.500 --> 01:07:19.280
I am so sorry, but thank you.

1324
01:07:19.500 --> 01:07:20.700
Thank you for sharing with us.

1325
01:07:21.160 --> 01:07:23.960
Jenna, I feel like Kate needs an office lady's coffee mug.

1326
01:07:24.080 --> 01:07:26.140
I mean, she lost her tooth.

1327
01:07:26.780 --> 01:07:27.260
Yes!

1328
01:07:27.500 --> 01:07:27.920
Yes!

1329
01:07:28.140 --> 01:07:30.440
We have to send Kate a mug.

1330
01:07:30.820 --> 01:07:32.320
Kate, we're sending you a mug.

1331
01:07:32.540 --> 01:07:34.540
Thank you for your love of the office.

1332
01:07:35.060 --> 01:07:35.800
Big hugs.

1333
01:07:35.800 --> 01:07:42.140
Well, while all of this dancing is happening at the church, they cut back and forth between

1334
01:07:42.140 --> 01:07:46.300
the church and Jim and Pam getting married on Maid of the MiSt.

1335
01:07:46.600 --> 01:07:49.340
It just makes the whole moment that much more special.

1336
01:07:49.340 --> 01:07:50.240
I loved it.

1337
01:07:50.420 --> 01:07:51.400
I know.

1338
01:07:51.600 --> 01:07:55.420
Lady, let me tell you now about the Maid of the MiSt.

1339
01:07:56.060 --> 01:08:01.740
We kind of covered this a little bit with Greg, which is that we could only rent out

1340
01:08:01.740 --> 01:08:03.080
the front of the boat.

1341
01:08:03.080 --> 01:08:06.760
The rest of the boat was filled with paying customers.

1342
01:08:07.420 --> 01:08:14.040
The other thing was that we were in no way allowed to change the course of the boat or

1343
01:08:14.040 --> 01:08:15.560
the length of the boat ride.

1344
01:08:15.860 --> 01:08:23.780
So before we went out, Randy and Randall and Paul Feig had all scouted this boat trip.

1345
01:08:24.520 --> 01:08:31.740
They rode the boat over and over again to see exactly when they wanted Jim and Pam to exchange

1346
01:08:31.740 --> 01:08:37.340
vows to have the falls in the background, how long we had before the boat would turn, everything.

1347
01:08:38.100 --> 01:08:44.240
They sort of estimated that to cover it all, we would have to take eight boat trips.

1348
01:08:45.320 --> 01:08:52.340
So they also realized that depending on the time of day, there would be spray coming off the

1349
01:08:52.340 --> 01:08:58.220
falls, like some times of day or depending on the wind, you got more spray.

1350
01:08:58.440 --> 01:09:01.900
So when you get on the boat, everybody wears those like blue parkas.

1351
01:09:02.020 --> 01:09:03.480
They give them to you with your ticket.

1352
01:09:03.660 --> 01:09:04.220
Right, right.

1353
01:09:04.280 --> 01:09:05.440
Like the ones you get at Disneyland.

1354
01:09:05.860 --> 01:09:06.300
Exactly.

1355
01:09:06.560 --> 01:09:08.520
When it's raining, everyone has their poncho on.

1356
01:09:08.520 --> 01:09:09.380
Exactly.

1357
01:09:10.180 --> 01:09:13.540
So they were like, okay, we'll have them wear their little ponchos.

1358
01:09:13.600 --> 01:09:16.440
They'll take them off to go get the boat captain.

1359
01:09:16.600 --> 01:09:17.480
That's super cute.

1360
01:09:18.000 --> 01:09:19.480
They had it all figured out.

1361
01:09:19.660 --> 01:09:26.160
Randall was like, listen, I am going to need to shoot on a film camera because the white falls

1362
01:09:26.160 --> 01:09:27.320
are like really white.

1363
01:09:27.440 --> 01:09:29.900
I'm not going to be able to color balance on a digital camera.

1364
01:09:30.840 --> 01:09:34.560
That was like a whole extra thing, you know, to shoot on film instead of digital.

1365
01:09:35.040 --> 01:09:39.460
But anyway, we were so limited in the number of people we could have in the front of the boat

1366
01:09:39.460 --> 01:09:46.100
that Greg asked Randy Cordray, our line producer, to play the minister, the boat captain.

1367
01:09:46.340 --> 01:09:49.760
So that's who you see marrying Jim and Pam.

1368
01:09:49.760 --> 01:09:52.360
And it warms my heart to see him.

1369
01:09:52.500 --> 01:09:53.880
I just love it so much.

1370
01:09:53.900 --> 01:09:54.162
I know.

1371
01:09:54.162 --> 01:09:54.500
I do too.

1372
01:09:54.500 --> 01:09:55.700
It makes me so happy.

1373
01:09:56.100 --> 01:10:01.580
But we also had a bunch of family members of our cast and crew in the front of the boat with us.

1374
01:10:01.580 --> 01:10:09.280
Greg Daniels' assistant, Mary Wall, is from the area, and her family volunteered to come ride the boat.

1375
01:10:09.640 --> 01:10:10.420
That's right.

1376
01:10:10.420 --> 01:10:15.020
If you listen to the DVD commentary, Mary is pointing out, she's like, that's my cousin.

1377
01:10:15.260 --> 01:10:16.380
That's so-and-so.

1378
01:10:16.780 --> 01:10:18.420
Like her whole family was in it.

1379
01:10:19.140 --> 01:10:24.020
Also, Kelly Hannon, who is one of our writer's assistants, her family rode the boat.

1380
01:10:24.020 --> 01:10:29.320
And then the craziest thing was that Brian Baumgartner's parents, Bruce and Cherry,

1381
01:10:29.920 --> 01:10:32.560
happened to be on vacation in Rochester, New York.

1382
01:10:32.740 --> 01:10:37.600
And they told Brian they were going to visit Niagara Falls the same day we were shooting.

1383
01:10:37.900 --> 01:10:38.980
This is so crazy.

1384
01:10:39.200 --> 01:10:43.120
They actually just had this planned, unknowing that we were going to be there filming.

1385
01:10:43.560 --> 01:10:44.000
Yes.

1386
01:10:44.360 --> 01:10:47.000
And Brian was like, well, you should stop by the set.

1387
01:10:47.180 --> 01:10:49.820
So he texted us, and we were like, oh, my gosh.

1388
01:10:49.960 --> 01:10:53.380
And then Paul Feig talked them into coming on the boat with us.

1389
01:10:53.380 --> 01:10:55.300
They did not know what they were getting into.

1390
01:10:55.600 --> 01:11:00.160
They are directly behind Jim and Pam as you guys walk on the boat.

1391
01:11:00.640 --> 01:11:01.020
Yes.

1392
01:11:01.480 --> 01:11:07.180
So let me just say, as we get out there, they warned us, you might get a little wet.

1393
01:11:09.220 --> 01:11:17.280
Lady, lady, as we took our first trip to the falls, we're getting closer, a little bit of spray.

1394
01:11:18.180 --> 01:11:23.160
All of a sudden, like, I don't even know what to call it.

1395
01:11:23.160 --> 01:11:25.000
Like, a tidal wave of water.

1396
01:11:25.240 --> 01:11:28.840
Like, sheets of water hit me.

1397
01:11:29.300 --> 01:11:36.000
Similar to the water cannon that hit me when I was an extra on the Universal Studios Jurassic Park ride.

1398
01:11:36.180 --> 01:11:38.720
Just like so much water.

1399
01:11:38.980 --> 01:11:42.160
Kelly Cantley said on the DVD commentary, Jenna,

1400
01:11:42.160 --> 01:11:53.080
it looked like someone took an enormous, full, giant tub of water and just doused you with it.

1401
01:11:53.180 --> 01:11:58.300
She said they could not believe how drenched you got in a matter of seconds.

1402
01:11:58.300 --> 01:11:59.820
You were drenched.

1403
01:11:59.820 --> 01:12:05.520
I will never forget John Krasinski's face after whatever that was hit me.

1404
01:12:05.760 --> 01:12:06.860
That spray hit me.

1405
01:12:07.100 --> 01:12:12.440
He, I knew how wet I was because of how he was looking at me.

1406
01:12:13.440 --> 01:12:19.160
And he sort of turned to them like, are we, I mean, can we continue?

1407
01:12:19.160 --> 01:12:24.900
She, is this, she looks like someone just tossed her over the side of the boat.

1408
01:12:25.240 --> 01:12:25.800
Yes.

1409
01:12:26.100 --> 01:12:28.440
My makeup was running down my face.

1410
01:12:29.060 --> 01:12:31.440
So, they just shot us from behind.

1411
01:12:31.440 --> 01:12:33.400
And actually, for that trip.

1412
01:12:33.580 --> 01:12:39.560
And you know that beautiful shot at the very end of the montage where my head is on John's shoulder?

1413
01:12:39.860 --> 01:12:40.040
Yeah.

1414
01:12:40.100 --> 01:12:42.520
That is because I could not turn around.

1415
01:12:42.760 --> 01:12:44.000
Because you were so soaked.

1416
01:12:44.000 --> 01:12:45.100
I was so soaked.

1417
01:12:45.660 --> 01:12:47.360
So, they brought us back to shore.

1418
01:12:48.680 --> 01:12:51.280
And they dried me off the best they could.

1419
01:12:51.460 --> 01:12:52.920
Like, on the side of the shore.

1420
01:12:53.400 --> 01:12:55.100
They sent us back out again.

1421
01:12:55.300 --> 01:12:56.920
The same thing happened again.

1422
01:12:57.700 --> 01:12:59.080
They were like, oh, no.

1423
01:12:59.240 --> 01:13:00.620
I don't know what to do.

1424
01:13:01.200 --> 01:13:02.940
I guess this is what we have.

1425
01:13:03.820 --> 01:13:06.660
Finally, in the afternoon, we went out again.

1426
01:13:07.120 --> 01:13:10.700
Hoping, like, maybe, you know, like, it'll be drier this time.

1427
01:13:11.660 --> 01:13:18.600
And Randy got to talking to the real boat captain, who was like, your actors got pretty drenched this morning.

1428
01:13:18.880 --> 01:13:20.720
And Randy was like, yes, yes.

1429
01:13:20.880 --> 01:13:25.320
But, you know, we were told that you cannot change course at all.

1430
01:13:25.560 --> 01:13:27.000
So, we're going to deal with it.

1431
01:13:27.060 --> 01:13:28.720
And the boat captain said, who said that?

1432
01:13:29.060 --> 01:13:30.560
I'm the captain of this ship.

1433
01:13:30.580 --> 01:13:32.340
And I'm a huge fan of the office.

1434
01:13:32.560 --> 01:13:34.160
I'll take you anywhere you want.

1435
01:13:34.500 --> 01:13:34.800
What?

1436
01:13:35.100 --> 01:13:36.940
And Randy was like, wait, what?

1437
01:13:37.280 --> 01:13:38.600
And he was like, that's right.

1438
01:13:38.600 --> 01:13:40.800
He goes, I just won't get so close this time.

1439
01:13:41.180 --> 01:13:43.320
So, he, he, like, stopped the boat.

1440
01:13:43.500 --> 01:13:45.840
So, you were out of, like, the splash zone.

1441
01:13:46.320 --> 01:13:46.760
Yes.

1442
01:13:47.000 --> 01:13:50.600
And that is how we ultimately were able to get a dry take.

1443
01:13:51.300 --> 01:13:52.520
So crazy, right?

1444
01:13:52.960 --> 01:13:55.920
Well, it all worked out because it's such beautiful footage.

1445
01:13:56.420 --> 01:13:58.520
You know, there's one thing that did not work out.

1446
01:13:58.840 --> 01:13:59.280
What?

1447
01:13:59.640 --> 01:14:03.760
We got a fan question from April End in South Bend, Indiana, who noticed.

1448
01:14:04.380 --> 01:14:07.800
What's with the cheek kiss after the maid of the mist ceremony?

1449
01:14:08.800 --> 01:14:14.080
Did you notice that on Maid of the Mist, John kisses me on my cheek and not my lips?

1450
01:14:14.860 --> 01:14:15.800
Yeah, I do.

1451
01:14:15.820 --> 01:14:18.780
And I was like, what's, uh, why, why don't Jim and Pam want to kiss?

1452
01:14:19.000 --> 01:14:19.920
What's happening?

1453
01:14:20.340 --> 01:14:24.960
I will tell you, John Krasinski had a terrible flu.

1454
01:14:26.260 --> 01:14:29.220
Like, truly, you guys, he was running a fever.

1455
01:14:29.840 --> 01:14:38.500
Like, he showed up in hair and makeup that morning, and he was like, you know how, like, you're all clammy and glassy-eyed when you're really sick?

1456
01:14:39.100 --> 01:14:40.000
That was John.

1457
01:14:40.000 --> 01:14:42.440
He was having a hard time keeping food down.

1458
01:14:42.680 --> 01:14:43.480
Oh, my gosh.

1459
01:14:43.560 --> 01:14:46.340
And I'm sure you guys were like, we only have one day here.

1460
01:14:46.420 --> 01:14:47.160
What do you do?

1461
01:14:47.360 --> 01:14:48.240
You have to rally.

1462
01:14:48.760 --> 01:14:50.340
We had to shoot it.

1463
01:14:50.720 --> 01:14:53.680
First of all, to John's credit, you would never know he was sick.

1464
01:14:53.800 --> 01:14:54.680
He was so amazing.

1465
01:14:55.200 --> 01:14:56.500
He was such a trooper.

1466
01:14:56.880 --> 01:15:00.760
But he was really, really worried about giving me his flu.

1467
01:15:01.180 --> 01:15:05.460
And he was kind of like, I am not going to kiss her on the lips and give her this flu.

1468
01:15:05.660 --> 01:15:06.580
That is terrible.

1469
01:15:06.580 --> 01:15:07.400
I won't do it.

1470
01:15:07.620 --> 01:15:09.200
And I'm sure you were like, thank you.

1471
01:15:09.480 --> 01:15:10.200
I was.

1472
01:15:10.200 --> 01:15:12.160
I was like, okay, but we didn't know.

1473
01:15:12.340 --> 01:15:13.380
Like, what are we going to do?

1474
01:15:13.780 --> 01:15:26.080
So in editing, Claire had the idea that she would cut from the kind of fakie cheek kiss to a really good, real kiss back at the church ceremony.

1475
01:15:27.260 --> 01:15:29.940
And we just kind of hoped no one would notice.

1476
01:15:30.560 --> 01:15:35.800
It's true, though, because everyone is waiting for that magical kiss after they say, I do.

1477
01:15:36.160 --> 01:15:36.500
Yeah.

1478
01:15:36.760 --> 01:15:38.500
And the church one is such a good one.

1479
01:15:38.500 --> 01:15:42.340
And this all leads to this beautiful talking head by Jim.

1480
01:15:42.640 --> 01:15:46.180
Greg shared with us that he assigned the talking head to Danny Chun.

1481
01:15:46.700 --> 01:15:47.840
It's so lovely.

1482
01:15:47.840 --> 01:15:48.940
I think we should hear it.

1483
01:15:49.340 --> 01:15:52.680
I bought those boat tickets the day I saw that YouTube video.

1484
01:15:53.640 --> 01:15:55.260
I knew we'd need a backup plan.

1485
01:15:55.380 --> 01:15:57.560
The boat was actually plan C, the church.

1486
01:15:57.940 --> 01:15:58.460
It was plan B.

1487
01:15:58.900 --> 01:16:03.020
And plan A was marrying her a long, long time ago.

1488
01:16:04.720 --> 01:16:06.020
Pretty much the day I met her.

1489
01:16:07.200 --> 01:16:13.340
And Claire Scanlon, our editor, shared that she fought really hard to keep this talking head in.

1490
01:16:13.660 --> 01:16:17.200
And she shared maybe if it would have been one of the guys, it might have gotten cut.

1491
01:16:17.340 --> 01:16:19.940
Because everyone did think the wedding ended on such a high note.

1492
01:16:20.280 --> 01:16:22.680
But she just loved this talking head.

1493
01:16:22.840 --> 01:16:25.080
And I think it's so great that it stayed in.

1494
01:16:27.180 --> 01:16:41.520
And once again, our writers did that amazing thing they do where you go from this incredibly sweet moment to Kevin putting his feet in the ice machine at the hotel.

1495
01:16:41.520 --> 01:16:48.000
And then, to Michael and Pam's mom sneaking into a hotel room together.

1496
01:16:48.340 --> 01:16:48.920
Yes!

1497
01:16:49.100 --> 01:16:49.380
What?

1498
01:16:49.780 --> 01:16:50.240
What?

1499
01:16:51.020 --> 01:16:54.280
And that is how Niagara ends, you guys.

1500
01:16:54.960 --> 01:16:56.140
Oh, wow.

1501
01:16:56.140 --> 01:16:58.820
What fun re-watching this episode.

1502
